====================================================================================================
[L] R5 PREDICTION, made robust to the singular low-|g| tail
====================================================================================================
  Where whitening SENDS correction: the low-|g| cells. Their geography:
    in-window                base  8.44%  bottom-decile-|g|   1.8%  enrichment x0.21
    upstream x<0             base 32.14%  bottom-decile-|g|  33.6%  enrichment x1.04
    above shear layer y>2    base 69.60%  bottom-decile-|g|  90.0%  enrichment x1.29
    downstream x>6 & y<=2    base 13.60%  bottom-decile-|g|   6.0%  enrichment x0.44
  NOTE: a |g|^p ranking is DEGENERATE as a prediction -- for p>0 the top decile is
  invariant under any monotone map of |g| (so p=1 and p=0.5 give the same G2), and
  for p<=0 it is decided by the near-zero tail of |g|. The robust statement is the
  one above: whitening sends correction toward the LOW-|g| cells, which are 90.0%
  above the shear layer and 1.8%% in-window, so G2 falls. The two supporting
  measurements that do not rely on any first-order argument:
    G2(|beta_final-1|) = 26.86% < G2(|g|) = 35.38% -- the converged inversion is
  ALREADY less window-concentrated than its own sensitivity map; and the in-window
  per-cell gain |beta-1|/|g| is 0.582x the global median against 1.322x downstream.
  The 26.86%% actually achieved already sits
  BELOW the p=1 prediction of 35.38%, i.e. the converged inversion is already less
  window-concentrated than its own sensitivity map.

